// enc_sampler.c — X4 encoder drain (TIM1 encoder mode) with DIR from hardware
// - Hardware counts X4; we IRQ on CC1/CC2 rising.
// - Direction from TIM1->CR1.DIR (optional flip via ENC_DIR_REVERSED).
// - Z handled first (IDX). We timestamp/capture CNT at the Z IRQ itself.
// - AB state is READ FROM GPIO each CC (no synthetic toggling for the model).
// - "AB since Z" (X4) is computed once in the ISR from CNT+DIR and mirrored to main.
// - A synthesized Gray stream is generated ONLY for printing traces, phase-locked at Z,
//   and stepped by DIR so prints show 0132 (FWD) / 0213 (REV) even with rising-edge-only IRQs.
// - Startup: Z is BLOCKED during warmup. We require both a min edge count and a min time before
//   exiting warmup (with a max timeout), then we drop the first few full windows to avoid "rushed"
//   first inferences. The old "steps since" is removed; keep "AB since Z (X4)" only.

